NNAAMMEE
     mkdir - make a new directory

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     mmkkddiirr _d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_y ...

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     mmkkddiirr creates each named _d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_y. For each _d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_y, it
     verifies that the parent directory exists and that the
     caller has write and search permission on it, then creates
     _d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_y itself together with the two entries .  and ..
     that every directory must contain: .  links to _d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_y it-
     self, and ..  links to its parent.

     Because only the superuser may create the underlying direc-
     tory node, mmkkddiirr is normally installed set-user-id to root;
     the new directory is then given to the invoking user with
     cchhoowwnn(), so that it is owned by the user who ran mmkkddiirr
     rather than by root.

     mmkkddiirr catches the SSIIGGIINNTT and SSIIGGHHUUPP signals while it works,
     so that an interrupt cannot leave behind a half-formed
     directory that lacks its .  or ..  entry.

DDIIAAGGNNOOSSTTIICCSS
     mmkkddiirr returns a nonzero exit status if any _d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_y could
     not be created, after printing one of the following com-
     plaints to the standard error:

     cannot get child dir name %s
          The last component of _d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_y could not be extracted
          from the pathname.

     %s not allowed
          The last component of _d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_y is .  or .., which can-
          not be created as a new directory.

     parent dir %s does not exist
          The directory that would contain _d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_y does not ex-
          ist.

     no permission to mkdir in %s
          The caller lacks write and search permission on the
          parent directory.

     %s already exists
          _d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_y (or a file of that name) is already present.

     not the super-user
          The underlying directory node could not be created be-
          cause mmkkddiirr is not running with superuser privilege.

     link to %s failed
          The .  or ..  entry could not be linked into the new
          directory; in this case mmkkddiirr removes the partially


